  "cause": "Existing common-type merge understood generated platform prefixes only. More precise Drone input and generic WorldObject input became a sticky type-conflict packet, losing cursor information. Comparing field names after that point would not recover a sound position contract.",
  "fix": "Pass the existing frozen policy explicitly through the single register/stored/state/call/counter-loop merge path. Its common-type operation follows canonical zero-offset custom parents to the nearest shared ancestor, including siblings, before conflict creation. Reuse canonical parent lookup; no field-name inference, target recognizer, extra state field, global registry or parallel solver.",
  "conservative_guards": [
    "Real unknown predecessors remain absorbing, in either input order.",
    "Mismatched current cursor/array positions retain the existing loss of pointer/extent facts.",
    "Unrelated roots, mixed generated/custom domains and already-conflicted packets are not rescued.",
    "Only common-prefix members survive; subtype-only fields are lost.",
    "Pointer candidate, origin, entry-expression and merged-producer provenance semantics are unchanged. Common type does not mean equal address or safe lifetime.",
    "Generated platform-prefix behavior is unchanged. Existing declaration admission refuses unknown/cyclic/truncated/overlapping custom parents."
  ],
